xG_modelling.R
	I added a conditional block that checks whether the data was fetched and parsed with the R scraper or with my python scraper. It then calls the proper function in xG_preparation.R to create the "expanded" df with the new columns we expect. After that block, we should have the same (or very similar columns).

	In the spring and summer 2025, I fetched and re-parsed 2021 data with my Python repo -- and ultimately will likely do the same for the shorten 2020-2021 season -- such that I will eventually have no R parsed data for which I would not have the corresponding python data, so the R data will only be useful for reproducing the original model for comparison purposes.


