		data.table's shift() instead of dplyr's lag function:
			?shift

			There is a lag() function in stats but it seems to be specific to time-series objects and apparently is not well suited for by operations.

			data.table has a shift() function.

			Before changing lag() to shift() in fun.pbp_prep(), I created *_alt columns and checked them against the ones created with lag()

			browser()
			dt[ mask==TRUE,
				`:=`(
				seconds_since_last_alt  = game_seconds - shift(game_seconds),
				event_type_last_alt     = shift(event_type),
				event_team_last_alt     = shift(event_team),
				event_strength_last_alt = shift(game_strength_state),
				coords_x_last_alt       = shift(coords_x),
				coords_y_last_alt       = shift(coords_y)
				),
				by = .(game_id, period) ]

			identical( dt$seconds_since_last, dt$seconds_since_last_alt )
			identical( dt$event_type_last, dt$event_type_last_alt )
			identical( dt$event_team_last, dt$event_team_last_alt )
			identical( dt$event_strength_last, dt$event_strength_last_alt )
			identical( dt$coords_x_last, dt$coords_x_last_alt )
			identical( dt$coords_y_last, dt$coords_y_last_alt )

